Limbo Emulator (QEMU 11.1.3) for Android
================================================================================

1. What is this?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Limbo is a QEMU-based emulator for Android.  This fork upgrades the original
QEMU 5.1.0 integration to **QEMU 11.1.3** for arm64-v8a devices:

  * `libqemu-system-x86_64.so`  – the system emulator, dlopen()ed by the app
  * `libqemu-img.so`            – the block layer, used to create disk images
  * `liblimbo.so`               – JNI control plane + callbacks QEMU/SDL need
  * glib/pixman/SDL2/libslirp/libffi/zlib-ng/zstd/pcre2/libiconv – cross-built
    dependencies shipped in `jniLibs/arm64-v8a`

Only arm64-v8a is supported.  QEMU is built as a normal executable with meson
and then re-linked as a shared object; the app loads it at runtime.

The QEMU source tree is **not** committed.  All local changes are a patch
series under `limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni/patches/qemu-11.1.3/`, applied by
`make prepare`.  That directory is the authoritative record of every QEMU
change; regenerate the patches after editing `jni/qemu`, never edit the
downloaded tree and leave it there.

virgl/OpenGL acceleration (MobileGL) is not implemented in this build: QEMU is
configured with `--disable-opengl --disable-virglrenderer`.


2. Requirements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Host (Linux x86_64 is what was used):

    make autoconf automake libtool-bin pkg-config flex bison gettext
    python3 python3-venv cmake (>= 3.24) ninja-build meson patchelf curl git
    ccache (optional)

Android toolchain:

    Android NDK r30 (30.0.16248370), clang 21
    Android SDK platform 31
    Android SDK build-tools 35.0.0  (needed for `zipalign -P 16`)
    JDK 17
    Gradle 8.2.1

The workspace used for development looks like this (the app repo may live
anywhere, but `deps/`, `build/` and `prebuilt/` sit next to it by default):

    limbo/                       # workspace root (LIMBO_ROOT)
    ├── envsetup.sh              # interactive shell helper
    ├── deps/                    # source tarballs (see §5)
    ├── prebuilt/arm64-v8a/      # cross-built dependencies (PREFIX)
    ├── build/                   # native build trees and build outputs
    ├── android-ndk-r30/
    ├── android-sdk/
    ├── jdk-17/
    ├── gradle-8.2.1/
    └── limbo-dontknowhy/        # this repository
        ├── Makefile             # native + APK build
        ├── scripts/             # build scripts used by the Makefile
        ├── keystore/            # release signing key (see §9)
        └── limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni/
            ├── patches/qemu-11.1.3/   # QEMU patch series
            ├── patches/setjmp-aarch64/# bionic sigsetjmp replacement
            ├── limbo/, compat/        # liblimbo.so sources
            ├── qemu/ glib/ pixman/ SDL2/ libffi/  # extracted sources (ignored)

If your layout differs, pass `LIMBO_ROOT=`, `PREFIX=`, `BUILD=` or `DEPS=` to
make.  `scripts/env.sh` derives everything from its own location and honours
the same variables; `envsetup.sh` in the workspace root is a thin wrapper for
interactive shells:

    source ./envsetup.sh


3. Quick start
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    # one-time: fetch tarballs if deps/ is empty
    make -C limbo-dontknowhy deps-fetch

    # build everything and produce a signed release APK
    make -C limbo-dontknowhy apk

The result is `build/limbo-x86-qemu11-arm64-release.apk` (workspace `build/`,
not the repo's Gradle `build/`), 16 KB aligned and signed.  For day-to-day
iteration:

    make -C limbo-dontknowhy native      # dependencies + QEMU + liblimbo
    make -C limbo-dontknowhy apk-debug   # debug-signed APK

The historical entry point still works:

    cd limbo-dontknowhy/limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni
    make            # == make native
    make apk


4. Versions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    QEMU          11.1.3
    glib          2.90.1      (needs libffi, pcre2, libiconv, proxy-libintl)
    pixman        0.46.4
    SDL2          2.32.10
    zlib-ng       2.3.3       (ZLIB_COMPAT mode, installs libz.so)
    zstd          1.5.7
    pcre2         10.49
    libiconv      1.18
    libffi        3.4.3
    libslirp      4.9.7
    proxy-libintl 0.5         (glib subproject, built by glib)
    NDK           r30 / clang 21
    API           21 (minSdk), targetSdk 29
    ABI           arm64-v8a

Compile flags are pure armv8-a plus the optional extensions:

    -march=armv8-a+simd+crc+crypto -mtune=cortex-a76 -O3 -fPIC

NEON is part of the AArch64 baseline; the old `--disable-arm-neon` flags are
gone.  QEMU's release build uses **full LTO** (`-Db_lto=true
-Db_lto_mode=default`), which measured ~6-7% faster TCG than a non-LTO build
for ~4 MB more `.so`.

Extra optimisation flags were also benchmarked (the safe subset of the old
`build.sh`: `-fdata-sections -ffunction-sections -fmerge-all-constants
-fomit-frame-pointer -fno-semantic-interposition` + vectorisation; Polly,
libomp, libunwind and `-fno-emulated-tls` are deliberately not used).  On a
Xiaomi 2410DPN6CC with Alpine 3.24, 256 MB `dd if=/dev/zero bs=1M count=256 |
md5sum`, `taskset 40`, five runs each: baseline 6.64/6.63/8.36/8.33/6.67 s vs
optimised 6.66/6.68/6.67/8.38/6.66 s — inside the noise, and `.text` only
shrank by 1.4%.  They are therefore **not** enabled.  To repeat the
experiment: `EXTRA_CFLAGS="..." QEMU_BUILD=$BUILD/qemu-build-opt
scripts/qemu-configure.sh`, then build/relink as usual.

Polly *is* included in the NDK r30 clang and works for sequential
optimisation; only `-polly-parallel` is off the table because it pulls in
libomp, which this project does not ship.  A Polly build
(`-mllvm -polly -polly-vectorizer=stripmine -polly-invariant-load-hoisting
-polly-run-inliner -polly-run-dce -polly-detect-keep-going
-polly-ast-use-context`) configures and links fine, but measured **no gain**:
10 runs each of the dd|md5 benchmark gave baseline min 5.66 s / median 5.69 s
vs Polly min 5.68 s / median 5.72 s, i.e. within noise (TCG is a large switch
over computed gotos, not affine loop nests).  `.text` shrank only 1.3%.  It is
therefore not enabled.


5. Source tarballs (`deps/`)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The build extracts sources into `jni/` (QEMU/glib/pixman/SDL2/libffi) and
`build/src/` (the rest).  `scripts/fetch-deps.sh` downloads whatever is
missing and verifies sha256:

    qemu-11.1.3.tar.xz        https://download.qemu.org/
    glib-2.90.1.tar.xz        https://download.gnome.org/sources/glib/2.90/
    pixman-0.46.4.tar.xz      https://cairographics.org/releases/
    SDL2-2.32.10.tar.gz       https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/releases/
    libffi-3.4.3.tar.gz       https://github.com/libffi/libffi/releases/
    zlib-ng-2.3.3.tar.gz      https://github.com/zlib-ng/zlib-ng/
    zstd-1.5.7.tar.gz         https://github.com/facebook/zstd/releases/
    pcre2-10.49.tar.gz        https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/releases/
    libiconv-1.18.tar.gz      https://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/libiconv/
    proxy-libintl-0.5.tar.gz  https://github.com/frida/proxy-libintl/
    libslirp-4.9.7.tar.gz     https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/slirp/libslirp/

`git clone` of libslirp v4.9.7 works too if you repack it, but use the
tarball: `git archive --prefix=libslirp-4.9.7/ v4.9.7`.  4.9.0 does **not**
link with lld (its version script fails); 4.9.7 is required.

No host library is ever picked up: the meson cross files set
`pkg_config_libdir=$PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig` and QEMU is configured with
`PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR` pointing at the same directory.


6. QEMU patch series
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`jni/patches/qemu-11.1.3/` (apply in order; `make prepare` does it):

    0001-android-build-meson.patch
        meson/configure fixes for bionic: no librt/shm_open, never probe X11,
        skip signalfd/ivshmem, build util/limbo-openpty.c, define
        SDL_MAIN_HANDLED in system/main.c.

    0002-android-libc-compat.patch
        Missing/divergent libc interfaces: /tmp and /var/tmp replacement paths,
        statx DIOALIGN, tellDir/seekDir (bionic has no telldir), SCSI/9p
        name clashes, openpty declaration, mmap_min_addr default (Termux
        workaround), `linux/soundcard.h`, no <glob.h>, and a shm_open()
        emulation backed by files in the app cache.

    0003-limbo-ui-hooks.patch
        Hooks used by the Android UI: VGA full repaint flag, tunable SDL/VNC
        refresh intervals, SDL scale hint, and the weak
        Android_JNI_SetVMResolution callback from sdl2-2d.

    0004-android-audio-backends.patch
        Native OpenSL ES and AAudio audio backends (`audio/openslesaudio.c`,
        `audio/aaudioaudio.c`, QAPI definitions, meson probes).  AAudio is
        loaded with dlopen("libaaudio.so") so the library still loads on
        API 21.  Both are output+input (microphone capture works).

    0005-qemu-img-inprocess.patch
        `limbo_img_create()`: calls bdrv_create() directly so the app can
        create qcow2/raw/vmdk/vdi/vhdx/qed/vpc/parallels images without
        going through qemu-img's main() and its exit() calls.

    0006-fdset-hotplug.patch
        `limbo_fdset_add()`: register a file descriptor with QEMU's fdset
        machinery without a monitor/SCM_RIGHTS, used for changing removable
        media while the VM is running.  (`-add-fd` only exists on the command
        line; QMP's add-fd needs SCM_RIGHTS.)

New QEMU files added by the series:

    audio/openslesaudio.c, audio/aaudioaudio.c, util/limbo-openpty.c

`patches/setjmp-aarch64/` is not a QEMU patch: it contains the AOSP
`sigsetjmp`/`siglongjmp` implementation that replaces bionic's.  bionic's
versions are PAC-signed and crash (SIGILL, ESR 0x72000000) when a coroutine
switches stacks/threads.  `scripts/link-qemu-so.py` links it with
`--whole-archive` and binds QEMU's internal references with
`-Bsymbolic-functions`.

Regenerating the patches after changing `jni/qemu`:

    cd /tmp && rm -rf qemu-pristine && tar -xf $LIMBO_ROOT/deps/qemu-11.1.3.tar.xz
    # ... create the per-topic diffs, then verify they apply cleanly:
    cd /tmp/qemu-pristine && for p in $JNI/patches/qemu-11.1.3/*.patch; do
        patch -p1 < "$p"; done
    # the result must be identical to $JNI/qemu


7. Build
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All targets are in the app-level `Makefile`:

    make prepare      extract sources, apply QEMU patches, generate cross file
    make deps         zlib-ng -> zstd -> pcre2 -> libiconv -> libffi -> glib
                      -> pixman -> libslirp -> SDL2, installed into $PREFIX
    make liblimbo     jni/limbo + jni/compat -> jniLibs/arm64-v8a/liblimbo.so
    make qemu         QEMU configure + ninja + re-link -> libqemu-system-*.so
    make native       all of the above
    make jnilibs      copy the dependency .so files into jniLibs
    make apk          release APK (see §9)
    make apk-debug    debug APK

Stamps live in `build/.stamps/`; delete one (or `make distclean`) to force a
step to run again.

Manual equivalents, if you want to see what the Makefile does:

    # dependencies (meson example: glib)
    meson setup build/glib-build $JNI/glib \
        --cross-file build/config-meson.cross --prefix=$PREFIX \
        --buildtype=release -Dtests=false -Dintrospection=disabled ... 
    ninja -C build/glib-build install

    # QEMU
    scripts/qemu-configure.sh          # writes build/qemu-build
    ninja -C build/qemu-build qemu-system-x86_64 qemu-img
    python3 scripts/link-qemu-so.py build/qemu-build \
        qemu-system-x86_64 libqemu-system-x86_64.so
    python3 scripts/link-qemu-so.py build/qemu-build qemu-img libqemu-img.so
    scripts/fix-needed.sh jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libqemu-*.so

QEMU is configured through its own `configure` (it generates
`config-host.mak`, the target list and the meson cross file).  The important
switches are listed at the top of `scripts/qemu-configure.sh`; notable ones:

    --target-list=x86_64-softmmu
    --enable-sdl --audio-drv-list=sdl,opensles,aaudio
    --enable-vnc --enable-zstd --enable-iconv --enable-slirp
    --with-coroutine=sigaltstack --enable-trace-backends=nop
    --disable-opengl --disable-virglrenderer
    -Db_lto=true -Db_lto_mode=default

`coroutine_backend=sigaltstack` is required: bionic has no ucontext and the
sigaltstack backend is the one that works with the setjmp replacement.


8. Relinking and DT_NEEDED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

QEMU 11 has no Makefile.target hook, so `scripts/link-qemu-so.py` parses
`build.ninja`, takes the object list and `LINK_ARGS` of the `qemu-system-*`
and `qemu-img` edges and re-links them with `-shared`.  Object order matters
(objects before archives).  The script adds:

    -Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384     # 16 KB page devices
    -Wl,--whole-archive libandroid-setjmp.a -Wl,--no-whole-archive
    -Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions
    -Wl,--no-as-needed -llimbo -Wl,--as-needed     # QEMU only

The `--no-as-needed -llimbo` is important: `Android_JNI_SetVMResolution` is a
*weak* reference, so the default `--as-needed` drops `liblimbo.so` from
`DT_NEEDED`, and on bionic a dlopen'ed library only resolves against its own
`DT_NEEDED` set — the callback would silently stay NULL and SDL would never
report resolution changes to the UI.

The dependencies in `$PREFIX/lib` have normal sonames
(`libglib-2.0.so.0`, `libpixman-1.so.0`, ...) while Android packages the
files as `libglib-2.0.so`, `libpixman-1.so`, ...  `scripts/fix-needed.sh`
renames the `DT_NEEDED` entries with patchelf after linking (and
`scripts/sync-jnilibs.sh` copies the real files under the packaged names).

`jniLibs/arm64-v8a/` after a build:

    libSDL2.so libffi.so libgio-2.0.so libglib-2.0.so libgmodule-2.0.so
    libgobject-2.0.so libiconv.so libintl.so liblimbo.so libpcre2-8.so
    libpixman-1.so libqemu-img.so libqemu-system-x86_64.so libslirp.so
    libz.so libzstd.so

`libcompat-limbo.so` no longer exists; its two exported entry points
(`set_jni`, `Android_JNI_SetVMResolution`, plus `FileUtils.nativeAddFd`) are
part of `liblimbo.so`, which only needs liblog/libdl/libc.


9. APK packaging and signing
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`make apk` runs:

    gradle :limbo-android-x86:assembleRelease        # unsigned APK
    zipalign -P 16 -f 4 ...                          # 16 KB alignment
    apksigner sign --ks keystore/limbo-release.jks ... 
    zipalign -c -P 16 4 ... ; apksigner verify ...

Native libraries are stored **uncompressed** (`useLegacyPackaging = false`).
Android 15+ requires uncompressed `.so` files to be 16 KB aligned inside the
APK and every ELF LOAD segment to be 16 KB aligned; the NDK r30 toolchain and
the explicit `-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384` handle the ELF side, while
`zipalign -P 16` (build-tools 35.0.0 or newer) handles the ZIP side.  Older
zipalign (33/34) only knows `-p` (4 KB) and will leave the warning in place.

Signing key: `keystore/limbo-release.jks` with `keystore/keystore.properties`
(passwords in clear text).  This is a **published demo key** so that every
build of this fork upgrades the previous one; do not reuse it for anything
else.  `make keystore` regenerates it if you delete both files, but then
existing installs must be uninstalled first (signature mismatch).

Output: `build/limbo-x86-qemu11-arm64-release.apk`.

Installing on a device:

    adb install -r build/limbo-x86-qemu11-arm64-release.apk

On MIUI, `adb install` is often rejected; use:

    adb push build/limbo-x86-qemu11-arm64-release.apk /data/local/tmp/limbo.apk
    adb shell pm install -r /data/local/tmp/limbo.apk


10. What changed in the app (QEMU 11 integration)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * `Config.java` / `VMExecutor` build QEMU command lines for 11.1.3 (46 CPU
    models, invalid legacy CPU strings removed, `battery.dat` path fixed).
  * SAF (`content://`) disks use QEMU's fdset: Java opens a `ParcelFileDescriptor`,
    clears `FD_CLOEXEC`, passes `-add-fd fd=N,set=S` and QEMU gets
    `file=/dev/fdset/S`.  `/proc/self/fd/N` does not work under scoped storage.
  * `-kernel`/`-initrd` cannot use fdsets (QEMU uses fopen/mmap by path); the
    files are copied into `cache/limbo/saf-*.bin` first.
  * Running-VM media changes call `FileUtils.nativeAddFd` -> `limbo_fdset_add()`
    in libqemu; QMP is not needed.
  * Firmware/ROM assets are QEMU 11.1.x; `FileInstaller` validates their size
    and CRC32 and refreshes them when the app's asset tag changes.  `.fd`
    files are only size-checked because QEMU writes NVRAM variables into them.
  * Only one `-pflash` may be attached (32- vs 64-bit UEFI); both together
    exceed `vm.max_map_count` and cause Scudo OOM.
  * Audio uses the new OpenSL ES/AAudio backends for both SDL and VNC display
    modes, with microphone capture.
  * Screen saver (DVD logo + immersive mode) and the special-keys bar are app
    features, described in the changelog/memo.
  * QEMU can only be initialised once per process; after stopping a VM the app
    must be restarted before starting another one.


11. Known issues
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * virgl/OpenGL (MobileGL) is not wired up.
  * Stop/start in the same process is not possible (`qemu_init` is one-shot).
  * The RenderThread Scudo crash seen once during UI teardown was never
    reproduced.
  * `qemu-img` can create qcow2/raw/vmdk/vdi/vhdx/qed/vpc/parallels; bochs,
    cloop and dmg can only be opened/converted, not created.
  * OpenSL ES/AAudio are S16; the requested rate/channel count is downgraded
    automatically if the device does not support it (mixeng resamples).


12. Debugging notes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * QEMU logs: `cache/limbo/qemu.log` inside the app data directory.
  * `build/logs/` in the workspace holds the build logs.
  * Device-side harness without installing the app: `build/tools/limbo-smoke`
    is an arm64 binary that dlopen()s a QEMU .so and forwards its argv to
    `qemu_init`.  Run it as the shell user from `/data/local/tmp` (SELinux
    forbids executing binaries from the app's private directory) with the
    app's lib directory in `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`.
  * The emulator refuses to start if `libqemu-system-*.so` cannot be dlopen'ed:
    check `DT_NEEDED` with `llvm-readelf -d` and make sure every dependency is
    present in `jniLibs/arm64-v8a` under the packaged name.
  * `zipalign -c -P 16 4 app.apk` must print "Verification successful".


